<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Drougoubitai</h1><p class="st-meta">615 CE – 850 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Slavic tribe west of Thessalonica that besieged the city in the 7th century and later gave its name to a Byzantine bishopric.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Drougoubitai settled in the plain west and north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a>, towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar">Vardar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pelagonia">Pelagonia</a>, in the early 7th century. They appear in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miracles-of-saint-demetrius">Miracles of Saint Demetrius</a> among the tribes that attacked Thessalonica.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from Byzantine sources, they lived under their own chiefs and alternated between hostility and alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a>, at times supplying the city with grain. In the 680s they were involved in the affair of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuver">Kuver's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a>, who settled near them.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the 9th century the southern Drougoubitai were within Byzantine rule, with a bishopric of Drougoubiteia, while northern lands fell to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a>. The tribe then disappears as a distinct group.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 615 CE – 850 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:71.94%;width:4.68%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>615 CE – 850 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Slavic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a>, <a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dragovites, Dragovichi (Balkan)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=732&amp;focus=drougoubitai" aria-label="Drougoubitai on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5222 771 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Drougoubitai lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5542 1027h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5542 1027h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Greece. <a href="/atlas?year=732&amp;focus=drougoubitai">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

